# Times are container-local (TZ=America/Chicago, set in the Dockerfile).
# Supercronic does not overlap a job with itself, so a 40-minute render blocks
# the next produce-next firing rather than stacking one up behind the lease.
# Paths and env come from the compose service; there is no PATH/cd preamble
# because supercronic is not cron and does not run with a bare environment.

# Scout trends into the topic queue, staggered 5 minutes off the hour so it
# never co-fires with produce-next — defense in depth on top of the DB
# busy_timeout, since both processes write one SQLite file.
5 7,12,17 * * * pnpm brainrot scout

# One unit of production per tick: resume one blocked job, or produce one video.
*/25 * * * * pnpm brainrot produce-next

# One publish attempt per tick, on whichever due slot is furthest behind its
# channel's cadence. Deliberately NOT staggered off produce-next: the two touch
# disjoint rows and WAL plus busy_timeout make a same-minute co-fire safe.
*/15 * * * * pnpm brainrot publish-next

# Daily report. Its only delivery is the container log stream.
0 8 * * * pnpm brainrot digest
